        <div class="docs-content">
            <section id="overview">
                <h2>Overview</h2>
                <p>Query Gate is a .NET 10 Blazor Server application backed by PostgreSQL for governed database access across PostgreSQL, SQL Server, MySQL and MariaDB. Users work in a query workspace without seeing database credentials. Permissions, approvals and audit records control and document every execution.</p>
                <p>Key capabilities: permission-gated SQL with ScriptDom AST parsing, multi-engine support, granular object-level scoping and role boundaries, dynamic PII data masking (HIPAA, GDPR, PCI-DSS, SOC 2), visual query execution plans, time-boxed access grants, audit-first execution, passkey / TOTP authentication, an access-request workflow, and multi-format exports (CSV, Excel XLSX/XLSB, JSON, Markdown, and SQL INSERT scripts).</p>
            </section>

            <section id="first-steps">
                <h2>First steps</h2>
                <p>Once deployed, create your administrator account on the setup screen or via optional environment variables on first start.</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Complete the initial setup wizard to create your root administrator account.</li>
                    <li>Register a target database (SQL Server, PostgreSQL, MySQL, or MariaDB) using a dedicated, least-privilege account.</li>
                    <li>Create users and grant permissions or review their access requests.</li>
                    <li>Open the query workspace to run permitted SQL and review activity in the audit log.</li>
                </ol>
            </section>

            <section id="user-guide">
                <h2>User guide</h2>
                <p>Query Gate provides engineers and auditors with controlled database access while eliminating credential sprawl.</p>
                <div class="docs-guide-cards">
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="terminal" /> Query workspace</h3>
                        <p>Select your database, write SQL with Monaco syntax assistance and keyboard shortcuts (<kbd>F5</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl+Enter</kbd>), and execute queries. Results appear in a responsive, filterable data grid with row counters.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="shield" /> SQL Gate validation</h3>
                        <p>Queries are parsed and verified using Microsoft ScriptDom (and dialect parsers) before execution. Disallowed statements, cross-database queries, or forbidden system procedures are denied upfront.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="key" /> Access requests &amp; approval</h3>
                        <p>Need temporary or elevated access? Request access directly from the Access page. Administrators review, approve with expiration dates, or reject requests with full audit records.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="download" /> Auditing &amp; multi-format export</h3>
                        <p>Every executed statement is recorded with duration, outcome, and user identity. Users with <code>EXPORT</code> permission can download query results as CSV, Excel (.xlsx, .xlsb), JSON, Markdown, or SQL INSERT statements.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="db" /> Object scoping &amp; boundaries</h3>
                        <p>Configure granular table and schema boundaries at both database and team-role levels. Protect sensitive tables with exclusion rules and wildcards like <code>dbo.*</code> or <code>*.secrets</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="lock" /> Dynamic PII masking</h3>
                        <p>Columns matching PII patterns (credit cards, SSNs, patient names, medical IDs) are redacted automatically. Users with the high-risk <code>UNMASK</code> permission see plain data.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="table" /> Results grid &amp; live aggregates</h3>
                        <p>Drag column dividers to resize, inspect real-time statistics (Count, Distinct, Sum, Avg, Min, Max) on the sticky aggregates bar, and double-click any cell to inspect JSON and XML with auto-formatting.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="folder" /> Deep schema explorer</h3>
                        <p>Group tables and views by schema (dbo, sales, audit) or display as a flat list. Check <code>Cols</code> to search column names across all database tables directly from the filter bar.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="columns" /> Flexible workspace layout</h3>
                        <p>Toggle between stacked vertical and side-by-side horizontal workspace split layouts with smooth, bidirectional draggable divider resizing.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="docs-card">
                        <h3><Icon Name="search" /> Global command palette</h3>
                        <p>Press <kbd>Cmd+K</kbd> or <kbd>Ctrl+K</kbd> anywhere to search routes, switch databases with 1 click, toggle dark and light themes, or open new query tabs.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="parameterized-queries">
                <h2>Parameterized queries and Form Mode (No-Code Data Runner)</h2>
                <p>Query Gate supports parameterized SQL queries and can automatically generate interactive data entry forms for non-technical team members:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Supported parameter syntax:</b> Query Gate automatically recognizes parameters in three common syntaxes:
                        <ul>
                            <li>Colon prefix: <code>:userId</code>, <code>:startDate</code></li>
                            <li>At-sign prefix: <code>@@status</code>, <code>@@limit</code></li>
                            <li>Mustache brackets: <code>&#123;&#123;department&#125;&#125;</code>, <code>&#123;&#123;orderId&#125;&#125;</code></li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li><b>AST gate normalization:</b> Before parsing with ScriptDom or dialect gates, parameter tokens are safely normalized so that parameters inside WHERE, HAVING, and LIMIT clauses do not trigger AST syntax errors.</li>
                    <li><b>Native driver parameter binding:</b> Parameter values supplied by the user are bound as dynamic ADO.NET parameters (such as <code>NpgsqlParameter</code>, <code>SqlParameter</code>, or <code>MySqlParameter</code>). Values are never concatenated into the raw SQL string, preventing SQL injection vulnerabilities.</li>
                    <li><b>Form Mode runner:</b> Click <b>Form Mode</b> in the editor toolbar to switch into form mode. Query Gate generates input fields based on parameter names (datetime pickers for dates, number inputs for IDs/counts, text inputs for codes and names). Users enter values and click <b>Run Form</b> to execute without editing raw SQL.</li>
                    <li><b>Preview SQL drawer:</b> Non-technical operators can expand the <b>Preview Parameterized SQL Query</b> drawer to see how parameters map to the underlying statement, and click <b>Edit SQL</b> at any time to return to the Monaco editor.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="command-palette">
                <h2>Global Command Palette (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K)</h2>
                <p>Access navigation, database connections, and operational power tools from any page without touching the mouse:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Keyboard shortcut:</b> Press <kbd>Cmd+K</kbd> on macOS or <kbd>Ctrl+K</kbd> on Windows and Linux to open the command palette.</li>
                    <li><b>Instant navigation:</b> Type to filter routes across the Query Workspace, Dashboard, My Access, Approvals, Users, Databases, Settings, Matrix, and Audit logs.</li>
                    <li><b>Direct database switcher:</b> Search through managed databases and press Enter to navigate directly to the Query Workspace connected to that specific database.</li>
                    <li><b>Workspace actions:</b> Trigger theme toggling (Light / Dark mode), open new query tabs, or jump to documentation directly from the palette.</li>
                    <li><b>Keyboard navigation:</b> Use the Up and Down arrow keys to highlight items, Enter to select, and Escape to dismiss.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="visual-charting">
                <h2>1-Click visual charting for query results</h2>
                <p>Transform tabular query results into clean, interactive data visualizations directly inside the Query Workspace:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Zero external charting dependencies:</b> Charts are rendered as lightweight, responsive inline SVG elements directly in the browser, with no external CDN or heavy third-party libraries required.</li>
                    <li><b>Supported chart types:</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li><b>Bar chart:</b> Vertical bars with numerical Y-axis gridlines and value labels.</li>
                            <li><b>Line chart:</b> Trend lines with data point tooltips and connected vertices.</li>
                            <li><b>Area chart:</b> Smooth semi-transparent area graphs visualizing volume over categories.</li>
                            <li><b>Donut chart:</b> Proportional category slices with center metric totals.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li><b>Column mapping:</b> Use the Category Column (X-axis) and Value Metric (Y-axis) dropdowns to select which result set columns to visualize.</li>
                    <li><b>Multi-result set support:</b> Each result set in a multi-statement batch includes its own Visual Chart tab.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="team-library">
                <h2>Team Query Library and production safeguards</h2>
                <p>Collaborate on approved queries while enforcing strict safety boundaries when executing against critical production databases:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Team Query Library:</b> Save queries with a title, category tag (e.g. Finance, Customer Support, DevOps), and check <b>Share with Team &amp; Workspace</b> to make queries available to all workspace members.</li>
                    <li><b>Sidebar switcher:</b> In the left sidebar Saved panel, switch between <b>My Queries</b> (personal private queries) and <b>Team Library</b> (shared queries created by colleagues).</li>
                    <li><b>Production safeguard banner:</b> Whenever the active target database is designated as <code>Production</code>, a prominent high-visibility warning banner is rendered across the workspace.</li>
                    <li><b>Editor watermark:</b> A subtle <code>PRODUCTION</code> watermark overlay displays inside the editor pane to prevent accidental execution against live systems.</li>
                    <li><b>Destructive DML confirmation modal:</b> When a user initiates a destructive write statement (UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, TRUNCATE, ALTER) against a production database, a safety confirmation modal prompts the user to verify the database name or run as a safe rollback Dry-Run first.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="object-rules">
                <h2>Object-level scoping and boundaries</h2>
                <p>Query Gate allows administrators to restrict access not just per database, but down to specific schemas and tables:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Database-level rules:</b> Applied to all users querying a database. Excluded tables (e.g. <code>dbo.AuditLogs</code>, <code>*.passwords</code>) cannot be queried by anyone, even administrators.</li>
                    <li><b>Role-level rules:</b> Applied to members of specific roles (e.g. Developers, Support, QA). Whitelists allow querying only approved tables, while blacklists protect confidential tables.</li>
                    <li><b>Wildcard syntax:</b> Use <code>*</code> for all objects, <code>schema.*</code> for an entire schema (e.g. <code>sales.*</code>), or <code>*.column</code> / <code>*.table</code> for cross-schema matching.</li>
                    <li><b>Conflict prevention:</b> Query Gate automatically detects if an object is simultaneously included and excluded, preventing accidental misconfigurations.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="data-masking">
                <h2>Dynamic data masking and compliance</h2>
                <p>Query Gate includes built-in compliance presets aligned with major regulatory standards:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>PCI-DSS 3.4 &amp; 3.2:</b> Masks credit card PANs (preserving only last 4 digits) and completely redacts CVVs and PINs.</li>
                    <li><b>HIPAA Safe Harbor:</b> Redacts patient names (<code>J***n S***h</code>), medical record numbers (MRNs), admission dates, and geographic locations smaller than a state.</li>
                    <li><b>GDPR &amp; CCPA:</b> Redacts email addresses, IP addresses, government IDs, and telephone numbers.</li>
                    <li><b>SOC 2 Confidentiality:</b> Redacts employee salaries, compensation figures, and authentication secrets.</li>
                    <li><b>The UNMASK permission:</b> Marked as High Risk in the access matrix; required to view unredacted data. All unmasked queries are recorded in the audit trail.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="schema-pii-discovery">
                <h2>Automated schema PII discovery and masking recommendations</h2>
                <p>Prevent sensitive data exposure proactively by scanning database schemas for sensitive columns before queries are executed:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>In-app scanner:</b> Navigate to <b>Admin &rarr; Settings &rarr; Data Masking</b> and click <b>Scan Schema for PII</b>. Select any connected target database and click <b>Scan Schema</b>.</li>
                    <li><b>Heuristic compliance detection:</b> Analyzes table and column metadata against 11 compliance categories:
                        <ul>
                            <li>Credit card numbers and CVVs (PCI-DSS)</li>
                            <li>Social security and national identity numbers (GDPR, HIPAA)</li>
                            <li>Email addresses, phone numbers, and physical addresses (GDPR, CCPA)</li>
                            <li>Patient names and medical record numbers (HIPAA)</li>
                            <li>Birthdates, salaries, compensation, and authentication secrets (SOC 2)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li><b>Coverage analysis:</b> Results distinguish between columns already covered by existing active masking rules and unprotected columns.</li>
                    <li><b>1-Click protection:</b> For any unprotected column detected, click <b>Protect</b> to automatically create and activate an appropriate dynamic masking rule with zero manual regular expression authoring.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="ai-assistant">
                <h2>AI Assistant with policy guardrails (BYOAI)</h2>
                <p>Query Gate includes an integrated AI Query Assistant built on a strict <b>Bring Your Own AI (BYOAI)</b> model. Organizations connect their preferred AI infrastructure with zero data leakage guarantees.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Supported AI providers:</b> OpenAI (GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini), Google Gemini (Gemini 1.5/2.0), Anthropic Claude (Claude 3.5 Sonnet/Haiku), and local offline Ollama (llama3.2, mistral, etc.) via OpenAI-compatible endpoints.</li>
                    <li><b>Zero data leakage guarantee:</b> Query Gate transmits only compact database schema metadata (table names, column names, data types, primary keys, and foreign keys). <b>Table data rows and cell values are never sent to external AI providers.</b></li>
                    <li><b>AST policy guardrails:</b> Every query generated by the AI assistant is analyzed by Query Gate's AST <code>SqlGate</code> parser before being returned to the user. Destructive DDL (such as <code>DROP</code>, <code>TRUNCATE</code>, or <code>ALTER</code>) and unfiltered <code>UPDATE</code> or <code>DELETE</code> statements without <code>WHERE</code> clauses are immediately flagged with security warnings.</li>
                    <li><b>Natural language to SQL (Ctrl+I):</b> Press <code>Ctrl+I</code> (or click <b>AI Assistant</b> in the editor toolbar) to describe what query you need in plain English. The AI drafts dialect-specific SQL that you can insert, replace, or copy.</li>
                    <li><b>Explain and fix with AI:</b> When a query produces a syntax error or is rejected by the permission gate, click <b>Fix with AI</b> directly on the error banner to receive a plain-language explanation of the violation and a 1-click corrected SQL query.</li>
                    <li><b>AI plan explainer:</b> In the Execution Plan tab, click <b>Explain Plan with AI</b> to get an executive summary of performance bottlenecks, missing indexes, and tuning advice.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="er-diagrams">
                <h2>Interactive Entity-Relationship (ER) diagrams</h2>
                <p>Visualize table relationships directly in the Query Workspace without external desktop database modeling tools.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Focused neighborhood scope:</b> By default, the diagram renders the selected table and its immediate 1-hop or 2-hop foreign key relationships. This prevents visual clutter in large databases with hundreds of tables.</li>
                    <li><b>Full schema toggle:</b> Expand the diagram with one click to view all tables and relationships in the database.</li>
                    <li><b>Interactive SVG canvas:</b> Drag table cards to reorganize layouts with dynamic Bezier relationship arrow routing. Supports pan, mouse-wheel zoom, and fit-to-screen controls.</li>
                    <li><b>Schema introspection:</b> Inspect column types, nullability, primary key badges (<code>[PK]</code>), and foreign key badges (<code>[FK]</code>).</li>
                    <li><b>1-click query tab:</b> Click the <b>Query</b> button on any table card to instantly open a new workspace query tab populated with a dialect-specific <code>SELECT TOP 100</code> query.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="exports-and-plans">
                <h2>Exports and visual execution plans (DAG)</h2>
                <p>Query results can be exported into multiple formats, and execution plans can be inspected as interactive directed acyclic graphs (DAG):</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>CSV (.csv):</b> Standard comma-separated format with formula injection neutralization.</li>
                    <li><b>Excel (.xlsx &amp; .xlsb):</b> Native OpenXML and binary spreadsheet formats with styled header rows.</li>
                    <li><b>JSON (.json):</b> Formatted array of objects for API and developer integration.</li>
                    <li><b>Markdown:</b> Clean GitHub-flavored Markdown table copied directly to clipboard.</li>
                    <li><b>SQL INSERT script:</b> Generates runnable <code>INSERT INTO</code> scripts with optional idempotency (<code>IF NOT EXISTS</code>) checks based on selected primary/unique keys.</li>
                    <li><b>Interactive DAG operator tree:</b> View execution plans as a hierarchical operator flowchart with data flowing from child operators up to the root. Color-coded cost badges highlight operator costs (green for &lt;15%, yellow for 15-35%, red for &gt;35% bottlenecks).</li>
                    <li><b>Focus Bottleneck:</b> Instantly locate and inspect the most expensive operator in complex query plans.</li>
                    <li><b>3-way view toggle:</b> Seamlessly toggle between <b>Tree (DAG)</b>, <b>Operator Table</b>, and formatted <b>Raw XML/JSON</b>.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="sso-oidc">
                <h2>Enterprise Single Sign-On (OpenID Connect)</h2>
                <p>Query Gate supports OpenID Connect (OIDC) Single Sign-On, allowing teams to authenticate via their corporate identity provider while enforcing strict internal access controls.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Provider compatibility:</b> Integrates with Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD), Okta, Keycloak, Auth0, Google Workspace, and Ping Identity.</li>
                    <li><b>Strict authorized-only policy:</b> Open self-registration is disabled. Only pre-authorized, active users created by an administrator in <b>Admin &rarr; Users</b> can sign in via OIDC. Uninvited external users are automatically denied access.</li>
                    <li><b>Fail-closed audit logging:</b> All SSO authentication events, including successful logins and unauthorized attempts, are recorded in the central immutable audit log with client IP, user agent, and timestamp.</li>
                    <li><b>Configuration:</b> Configurable in <b>Admin &rarr; Settings &rarr; SSO &amp; OIDC</b> with automatic discovery via <code>/.well-known/openid-configuration</code> and AES-256 encrypted client secret storage.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="multi-tenancy">
                <h2>Multi-tenancy and workspaces</h2>
                <p>Query Gate supports multi-tenant workspaces with complete data isolation, allowing multiple independent organizations or departments to share a single platform deployment.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Path-prefix routing (/t/[slug]/):</b> Workspaces are accessed using a clean path prefix such as <code>/t/acme/dashboard</code> or <code>/t/marketing/query</code>. All navigation, query tabs, and administrative tools operate within that workspace context.</li>
                    <li><b>Custom domain mapping:</b> Map dedicated hostnames (such as <code>data.acme.com</code>) directly to a workspace. Query Gate resolves the tenant directly from the Host header with no path prefix required.</li>
                    <li><b>Row-level data isolation:</b> All tenant entities (databases, permission grants, audit logs, saved queries, query history, access requests, script requests, and environments) are strictly partitioned by <code>TenantId</code> using Entity Framework Core global query filters. Queries cannot read or write data across tenant boundaries.</li>
                    <li><b>Multi-tenant user memberships:</b> A single user account can belong to multiple workspaces with different roles in each (for example, Administrator in one workspace and Developer in another). Users can switch between workspaces using the topbar dropdown or the <code>/select-tenant</code> hub.</li>
                    <li><b>Tenant-isolated settings:</b> Each workspace maintains its own SMTP email server configuration, outgoing team notification webhooks (Slack, Teams, Discord, Zoho Cliq), and branding preferences.</li>
                    <li><b>Platform administration:</b> Users in the <code>SuperAdmin</code> role have access to <code>/platform/tenants</code> to provision workspaces, configure custom domains, toggle tenant access, and inspect global health. Platform administrators exist outside tenant data boundaries to preserve tenant privacy.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Setting up the SuperAdmin role</h3>
                <p>The <code>SuperAdmin</code> role unlocks platform-level management at <code>/platform/tenants</code>. There are two ways to assign this role:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>
                        <b>Bootstrap configuration (Recommended):</b> Set <code>BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL</code> and <code>BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> (or <code>BootstrapAdmin__Email</code> and <code>BootstrapAdmin__Password</code>). During startup, Query Gate automatically creates the user account (or finds the existing user) and assigns both <code>Admin</code> and <code>SuperAdmin</code> roles.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <b>Direct PostgreSQL SQL assignment:</b> If Query Gate is already running and you need to elevate an account immediately without restarting:
                        <div class="code-block-wrap" style="margin:12px 0">
                            <pre><code>-- Ensure the SuperAdmin role exists
INSERT INTO "AspNetRoles" ("Id", "Name", "NormalizedName", "ConcurrencyStamp")
VALUES (gen_random_uuid()::text, 'SuperAdmin', 'SUPERADMIN', gen_random_uuid()::text)
ON CONFLICT ("NormalizedName") DO NOTHING;

-- Assign SuperAdmin role to the user
INSERT INTO "AspNetUserRoles" ("UserId", "RoleId")
SELECT u."Id", r."Id"
FROM "AspNetUsers" u
JOIN "AspNetRoles" r ON r."NormalizedName" = 'SUPERADMIN'
WHERE u."NormalizedEmail" = UPPER('admin@company.com')
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p class="muted small">Sign out and sign back in after running the query to refresh authentication session claims.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>

                <h3>Workspace provisioning and user onboarding</h3>
                <p>To preserve tight security controls over internal database infrastructure, Query Gate disables public self-service signup. Workspaces and users follow an administrative workflow:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Provisioning a workspace:</b> A SuperAdmin navigates to <code>/platform/tenants</code>, clicks <b>Create Workspace</b>, and specifies the name, slug, contact email, plan, and initial administrator email.</li>
                    <li><b>Connecting custom domains:</b> Click <b>Domains</b> on any workspace row in <code>/platform/tenants</code> to bind a custom hostname (for example, <code>sql.acme.com</code>). Point your DNS CNAME or A record to the Query Gate host for direct host-based routing.</li>
                    <li><b>Adding users to a workspace:</b> Workspace administrators navigate to <b>Admin &rarr; Users</b> (<code>/admin/users</code>) and click <b>New user</b>. Existing platform accounts are associated with the workspace immediately, while new users receive a generated temporary password and must set their password upon initial sign in.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <!-- Grouped Deployment Section -->
            <section id="deployment" class="docs-section-group">
                <h2>Deployment options</h2>
                <p>Query Gate is a .NET 10 interactive server application backed by PostgreSQL. Interactive sessions use SignalR, which requires WebSocket support and HTTPS on remote hosts. Deploy Query Gate at the root of a domain name rather than a subpath. Choose the deployment option that fits your team's workflow and infrastructure:</p>

